[Lesson "hanging-pieces"]
[LessonTitle "Hanging pieces"]
[Step "explain"]
[TeacherNotes "Hanging means no friendly piece defends it | Always ask: what can the opponent take for free? | Check your own pieces as well as theirs"]
[Mistakes "Moving a piece and leaving another undefended | Not noticing that an attacked piece also attacks your piece"]
[ClassQuestions "Which pieces defend this one? | Who moves first, and does that change the answer?"]

{A hanging piece is a piece that nothing defends, so it can be taken for free.}
*

[Lesson "hanging-pieces"]
[Step "explain"]
[FEN "4k3/ppp2ppp/2n5/8/6b1/8/PPP2PPP/3Q2K1 w - - 0 1"]

{The black bishop attacks the white queen. But nothing defends the bishop! [%cal Rg4d1,Gd1g4] [%csl Rg4]}
1. Qxg4 {It is White's turn, so the queen takes the bishop for free.} *

[Lesson "hanging-pieces"]
[Step "quiz"]
[Question "What do we call a piece that no friendly piece defends?"]
[Choices "A hanging piece | A pinned piece | A forked piece"]
[Answer "1"]
[Explanation "A piece with no defender is hanging. The other side can capture it without losing anything back."]

*

[Lesson "hanging-pieces"]
[Step "find-move"]
[FEN "6k1/5ppp/8/8/3n4/8/5PPP/3R2K1 w - - 0 1"]
[Hint "Use your rook."]
[Hint "Take the knight on d4."]

{White to move. One black piece is hanging. Take it.}
1. Rxd4 {Nothing defends the knight, so White wins it for free. [%cal Gd1d4]} *

[Lesson "hanging-pieces"]
[Step "line-drill"]
[FEN "6k1/5ppp/8/8/3n4/8/5PPP/3R2K1 w - - 0 1"]
[Side "white"]
[Hint "Look for a black piece that nothing defends."]
[Hint "Your rook takes on d4."]

{Take the hanging knight as White.}
1. Rxd4 Kf8 *

[Lesson "defended-pieces"]
[LessonTitle "Is it defended?"]
[Step "explain"]
[TeacherNotes "Before you capture, count who can take back | A defended piece is not always safe to capture, but a trade of equal value can be fine | A queen should almost never take a defended pawn or minor piece"]
[Mistakes "Taking a pawn with the queen when a piece guards the pawn | Only looking at the piece you capture and not at what happens next"]
[ClassQuestions "Who can take back if I capture here? | How many points would I lose?"]

{Before you take a piece, ask: can it take back?}
*

[Lesson "defended-pieces"]
[Step "explain"]
[FEN "4k3/8/2b5/3n4/8/8/8/3QK3 w - - 0 1"]

{The white queen attacks the knight on d5. But the bishop on c6 defends the knight. [%cal Gd1d5,Rc6d5] [%csl Yd5]}
1. Qxd5 {The queen takes the knight.} 1... Bxd5 {The bishop takes back. White lost a queen for a knight. That is a bad trade.} *

[Lesson "defended-pieces"]
[Step "quiz"]
[Question "Can White safely take the pawn on e5 with the queen?"]
[Choices "Yes, it is a free pawn | No, the knight on c6 defends it"]
[Answer "2"]
[Explanation "After Qxe5+ the black knight on c6 takes the queen. White would lose a queen for a pawn."]

{White's queen attacks the pawn on e5.}
1. e4 e5 2. Qh5 Nc6 *

[Lesson "defended-pieces"]
[Step "find-move"]
[FEN "4k3/8/2b5/3n4/6b1/8/8/3QK3 w - - 0 1"]
[Hint "Use your queen."]
[Hint "The bishop on g4 has no defender."]

{White to move. One capture is safe and one is a mistake. Find the safe one.}
1. Qxg4 {The bishop on g4 had no defender. [%cal Gd1g4]} *

[Lesson "safety-check"]
[LessonTitle "Three questions before you move"]
[Step "explain"]
[TeacherNotes "Make the three questions a habit: What does my opponent attack? Is my target defended? Is this trade good for me? | Ask them out loud every move in class | Works for both colors"]
[Mistakes "Grabbing the first free-looking capture | Forgetting to check what the opponent attacks"]
[ClassQuestions "What does the white bishop attack? | Is the knight on d4 defended?"]

{Ask three questions: What does my opponent attack? Is my target defended? Is the trade good for me?}
*

[Lesson "safety-check"]
[Step "explain"]
[FEN "3qk3/8/8/6B1/3N4/2B5/8/4K3 b - - 0 1"]

{Black to move. The white bishop on g5 attacks the black queen. [%cal Rg5d8] [%csl Rd8]}
1... Qxd4 {This takes a knight, but the bishop on c3 defends it.} 2. Bxd4 {Black lost a queen for a knight. The three questions would have stopped this.} *

[Lesson "safety-check"]
[Step "find-move"]
[FEN "3qk3/8/8/6B1/3N4/2B5/8/4K3 b - - 0 1"]
[Hint "Use your queen."]
[Hint "Take the bishop on g5. Nothing defends it."]

{Black to move. Use the three questions, then find the safe capture.}
1... Qxg5 {The queen saves itself and wins a bishop. [%cal Gd8g5]} *
